-- title:
--   Lifting Fontaine-compatible points of unipotent p-divisible groups over ℤₚ
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $\mathcal O$ a commutative ring in which $p$ is a non-zero-divisor, equipped with an $\mathcal O$-algebra structure on $\mathbf Z/p$ whose structure map has kernel exactly $(p)$, and which is $(p)$-adically complete. Let $h\in\mathbb N$ and let $L$ be a family of commutative, cocommutative Hopf $\mathcal O$-algebras $L_v$, each finite and free over $\mathcal O$ with $\operatorname{finrank}_{\mathcal O}L_v=p^{vh}$, together with surjective bialgebra maps $t_v\colon L_{v+1}\to L_v$ whose kernel is the ideal generated by the image of the augmentation ideal $\ker(\text{counit})$ of $L_{v+1}$ under the $p^v$-th convolution power of the identity, and such that for every $v$ the Cartier dual $((\mathbf Z/p)\otimes_{\mathcal O}L_v)^\vee$ is a local ring. Fix $v$, and let $Y$ be a commutative $\mathcal O$-algebra, finite and free over $\mathcal O$. Let $\chi\colon (\mathbf Z/p)\otimes_{\mathcal O}L_v\to(\mathbf Z/p)\otimes_{\mathcal O}Y$ be a $\mathbf Z/p$-algebra map with the following property: for every $n$ and every truncated Witt vector $m$ of length $n$ over $(\mathbf Z/p)\otimes_{\mathcal O}L_v$ that is primitive (its image under the comultiplication equals the sum of its images under the two inclusions into the tensor square), if $m$ admits a lift to a Witt vector $X$ over $L_v$ with $(n-1)$-st ghost component in $p^nL_v$, then the image of $m$ under $\chi$ admits a lift to a Witt vector over $Y$ with $(n-1)$-st ghost component in $p^nY$. Then $\chi$ is the base change of an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism: there exists $x\colon L_v\to Y$ over $\mathcal O$ with $\mathrm{id}_{\mathbf Z/p}\otimes x=\chi$. Only existence of $x$ is asserted, and $x$ is merely an algebra map.
--
--   This is Fontaine's description of the points of a unipotent $p$-divisible group at finite level in the special case of residue field $\mathbf F_p$, i.e. $\mathcal O=\mathbf Z_p$: a point of the mod-$p$ fibre of $\Gamma_v$ with values in $(\mathbf Z/p)\otimes Y$ that respects the kernel of Fontaine's map $w$ on Witt vectors comes from a point over $\mathcal O$. It feeds the construction of Honda systems and of $p$-divisible towers used in the study of deformations of finite flat group schemes.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Deformation_exists_algHom_baseChange_eq_of_forall_map_mem_fontaineKer_of_forall_ker_eq_torsionIdeal_zmodp.lean

